/ActualText (Detail)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1549 0 R
/ActualText (1 Government allocation of emission permits)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
386 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1550 0 R
/ActualText (The government determines the total amount of carbon that can be emitted by each industrial sector and allocates carbon credits to companies accordingly. In this process, companies can receive a certain amount of emission permits for free from the government or purchase emission permits through an auction.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1551 0 R
/ActualText (2 Carbon emissions and monitoring)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1552 0 R
/ActualText (Companies carry out activities within the scope of their allocated emission permits, and regularly monitor and report the actual carbon emissions generated during this process.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1553 0 R
/ActualText (3 Trading of emission permits)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1554 0 R
/ActualText (Companies whose carbon emissions are less than their quota can sell their remaining credits on the market, and conversely, companies whose emissions exceed their quota must purchase additional credits. This helps companies manage their carbon emissions cost-effectively.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1555 0 R
/ActualText (4 Fines and Incentives)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1556 0 R
/ActualText (Companies that emit carbon in excess of their quotas may be subject to fines, and conversely, companies that effectively reduce carbon emissions may receive incentives from the government.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1557 0 R
/ActualText (5 Achieve carbon reduction goals)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1558 0 R
/ActualText (Through these mechanisms, governments and businesses strengthen cooperation to achieve national and international carbon reduction goals and pursue sustainable environmental management.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1559 0 R
/ActualText (6 Market-based adjustments)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1560 0 R
/ActualText (The carbon emissions trading system establishes a carbon price through a market-based mechanism, which encourages companies to invest more in technological innovation and efficiency improvement to reduce carbon emissions.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
